"""`aspect ci bazelrc` — write a Bazel rc block that configures vanilla `bazel`
calls to use Aspect's remote services and recommended optimizations.

`aspect <task>` injects its Bazel flags itself (see `feature/workflows.axl`,
`feature/deployment.axl`, and `get_bazelrc_flags` in `lib/environment.axl`). A
bare `bazel build` started from the same job gets none of that. This command
writes the equivalent into a Bazel rc file (`~/.bazelrc` by default — the first
user rc Bazel loads, picked up with no `--bazelrc` plumbing) so vanilla `bazel`
calls in the job pick up the same configuration.

It is the in-CLI successor to `rosetta bazelrc`: the CI integrations (the
setup-aspect GitHub Action, Buildkite plugin, CircleCI orb, GitLab component)
call this instead of `rosetta` once `rosetta` is gone from the runner image.

The rc gets two kinds of content:

  - Unconditional flags, applied to every `bazel` call. On a Workflows runner the
    full set — generic tuning, the remote-cache endpoint (from env), and the
    runner-specific flags (repository cache, per-runner output paths, identity
    header, the Workflows-cache compression gates). On other CI, or with an
    explicit `--output`: only the generic flags (plus the remote-cache endpoint
    when its env vars are set) — nothing tied to a runner's mounts or identity.

  - Opt-in `--config` sections, one per Aspect deployment this machine knows
    (`aspect auth status`) that advertises a remote cache or BES backend:

        --config=aspect-cloud          Aspect Cloud: remote cache + BES
        --config=aspect-<name>         a configured Aspect Workflows deployment
        --config=aspect-<name>-exec    the same, plus its remote execution
        --config=aspect                the default deployment (`aspect auth use`)
        --config=aspect-exec           the default deployment's `-exec` config

    Aspect Cloud's config takes its own name; a configured deployment `<name>`
    gets `aspect-<name>` (`aspect-cloud` and `aspect` are reserved names, so the
    two never collide). Each wires `--remote_cache` / `--bes_backend` /
    `--bes_results_url`, authenticates through the `aspect get` credential
    helper (scoped to the deployment's hosts), and — where BES is wired — asks
    Bazel for a complete stream: every action event, all BEP-referenced files
    uploaded, the compact execution log (Bazel >= 7.1), and no early exit before
    the upload finishes. Remote execution is never part of the base config: it
    relocates every action, so it is only ever reached by naming `-exec`,
    mirroring `--remote=exec` on `aspect <task>`. Aspect Cloud advertises no
    executor, so it gets no `-exec` config.

Off a runner and off CI with no `--output`, nothing is written, so a developer's
own `~/.bazelrc` is never clobbered.

The output is a marker-delimited managed block. An existing file keeps its other
content: the block replaces a previous one in place, or is appended when the file
has none — so an rc another setup step wrote survives, and re-running is
idempotent. A file consisting solely of an older (marker-less) `aspect ci bazelrc`
output is replaced whole.

On Bazel >= 6.3.0 flags are emitted under `common` (applies to every command);
older Bazel has no `common` pseudo-command, so they're spelled out under `build`
(inherited by test/run/coverage/cquery/aquery/fetch/…) and `query` (the one
action-relevant command that doesn't inherit `build`). Version-gated flags are
resolved against the detected Bazel version (assumed-latest when undetectable),
matching how the workflows feature gates the same flags at invocation time.

Only file output is supported — there is no stdout mode.
"""

load("@aspect//bazel/build_metadata.axl", "version_gte")
load("./private/lib/aspect_endpoint_auth.axl", "endpoint_host")
load(
    "./private/lib/environment.axl",
    "detect_ci",
    "error",
    "get_bazelrc_flags",
    "get_generic_bazelrc_flags",
    "get_workflows_environment",
    "info",
    "is_aspect_workflows_runner",
)

# Bazel gained the `common` pseudo-command (flags applied to every command) in
# 6.3.0. On older Bazel a `common` line is an unrecognized-command error, so we
# spell the flags out per command instead.
_COMMON_PSEUDO_COMMAND_MIN_VERSION = "6.3.0"

# The command sections used on Bazel < 6.3.0 (no `common`). `build` is inherited
# by the commands that matter here — test, run, coverage, cquery, aquery, fetch,
# clean, mobile-install, … — so listing it covers them all. `query` is the one
# action-relevant command that does NOT inherit `build`, so it's named
# explicitly. Every flag get_bazelrc_flags emits is accepted by `query` on Bazel
# < 6.3.0 (the only range this branch runs in), so emitting them all under both
# is safe — the flags that later Bazel rejects on `query` are gated to those
# newer versions, where we use `common` instead and never reach this path.
_PRE_COMMON_COMMANDS = ["build", "query"]

# Delimits the managed block in the rc file. `merge_managed_block` replaces
# whatever sits between them on the next run, so the text must stay stable.
BEGIN_MARKER = "# BEGIN aspect ci bazelrc"
END_MARKER = "# END aspect ci bazelrc"

# The first line of an rc written before the markers existed. That output was the
# whole file, so a file opening with it is still ours to replace.
_LEGACY_HEADER = "# Generated by `aspect ci bazelrc`"

# Bazel-facing Aspect endpoints are TLS gRPC.
_SCHEME = "grpcs://"

# Config name of the default deployment, and of the built-in Aspect Cloud entry
# (which takes its own name — see the module docstring).
DEFAULT_CONFIG = "aspect"
_CONFIG_PREFIX = "aspect-"
_EXEC_SUFFIX = "-exec"

# One `--config` section of the rc. `flags` are `str | (str, constraint)` like
# everywhere else; a plain `--config=<other>` entry chains to another section and
# is written as-is rather than version-resolved.
RcConfig = record(
    name = field(str),
    comment = field(str, default = ""),
    flags = field(list),
)

def _flag_str(flag) -> str:
    """A flag is either a plain string or, for a surviving version-gated option,
    a `(flag, version_condition)` tuple from `rc.expand` — take the flag text."""
    return flag[0] if type(flag) == "tuple" else flag

def is_config_chain(flag) -> bool:
    """Whether `flag` chains to another config section (`--config=<name>`).

    Public (not `_`-prefixed) so `bazelrc_test.axl` can load it."""
    return type(flag) == "string" and flag.startswith("--config=")

def startup_flags_for_rc(startup_flags: list) -> list:
    """Drop the rc-suppression startup flags, which are illegal inside an rc file.

    `get_bazelrc_flags` includes `--nohome_rc` and `--nosystem_rc` because the
    workflows feature passes these as *command-line* startup flags to
    `aspect <task>`. Here we write the flags into the home rc itself
    (~/.bazelrc), and Bazel rejects any `--no*_rc` option that appears inside a
    bazelrc with a fatal `Can't specify --nosystem_rc in the .bazelrc file`
    (likewise `--nohome_rc`, which would also be self-defeating — Bazel would be
    told to ignore the very file it's reading). These flags only suppress *other*
    rc files (`/etc/bazel.bazelrc`, `~/.bazelrc`); that's a command-line concern
    and there's nothing the generated rc can do about it, so we drop them here.

    Public (not `_`-prefixed) so `bazelrc_test.axl` can load it."""
    _RC_SUPPRESSION_FLAGS = ["--nohome_rc", "--nosystem_rc", "--noworkspace_rc"]
    return [f for f in startup_flags if f not in _RC_SUPPRESSION_FLAGS]

def command_sections(bazel_version: str | None) -> list:
    """The rc command sections the build flags go under. `common` (one section,
    applies to every command) on Bazel >= 6.3.0 or when the version is unknown
    (assume latest); the explicit `build`/`query` sections on older Bazel that
    has no `common` pseudo-command.

    Public (not `_`-prefixed) so `bazelrc_test.axl` can load it."""
    if bazel_version == None or version_gte(bazel_version, _COMMON_PSEUDO_COMMAND_MIN_VERSION):
        return ["common"]
    return _PRE_COMMON_COMMANDS

def config_name(deployment) -> str:
    """The `--config` name for a deployment summary: Aspect Cloud's own name for
    the built-in entry, `aspect-<name>` for a configured deployment.

    Public (not `_`-prefixed) so `bazelrc_test.axl` can load it."""
    return deployment.name if deployment.builtin else _CONFIG_PREFIX + deployment.name

def credential_helper_flags(hosts: list, helper: str) -> list:
    """`--credential_helper=<host>=<helper>` for each host, scoped so the helper is
    only ever invoked for a deployment's own endpoints, as version-gated tuples:
    Bazel 6.4.0 dropped the `experimental_` prefix (the old spelling still works
    there, with a deprecation warning), and 6.0.0 introduced the helper protocol.

    Public (not `_`-prefixed) so `bazelrc_test.axl` can load it."""
    flags = []
    for host in hosts:
        scoped = host + "=" + helper
        flags.append(("--credential_helper=" + scoped, ">=6.4.0"))
        flags.append(("--experimental_credential_helper=" + scoped, ">=6.0.0, <6.4.0"))
    return flags

def _dedupe(items: list) -> list:
    out = []
    for item in items:
        if item and item not in out:
            out.append(item)
    return out

def _login_hint(deployment) -> str:
    """How CI authenticates this deployment's config: its API-token variable,
    or the login command for a machine with a browser."""
    login = "aspect auth login" if deployment.builtin else "aspect auth login --deployment " + deployment.name
    if deployment.api_token_env:
        return "auth via " + deployment.api_token_env + " or `" + login + "`"
    return "auth via `" + login + "`"

def _label(deployment) -> str:
    return "Aspect Cloud" if deployment.builtin else "Aspect Workflows deployment '" + deployment.name + "'"

def deployment_configs(deployments: list, credential_helper: str, exec_log_path: str = "") -> list:
    """The `--config` sections for every deployment that advertises a remote cache
    or BES backend, in `deployments` order, followed by the `aspect` /
    `aspect-exec` aliases for the default one.

    `deployments` carries `aspect.DeploymentSummary` rows (or anything with the
    same `name` / `builtin` / `default` / `cache` / `bes` / `exec` /
    `results_url` / `api_token_env` fields). `credential_helper` is the path Bazel
    invokes as `<helper> get`. `exec_log_path`, when set, is where a BES-wired
    config writes the compact execution log for upload (Bazel >= 7.1).

    Public (not `_`-prefixed) so `bazelrc_test.axl` can load it.
    """
    configs = []
    aliases = []
    for d in deployments:
        if not (d.cache or d.bes):
            continue
        name = config_name(d)
        cache = endpoint_host(d.cache) if d.cache else ""
        bes = endpoint_host(d.bes) if d.bes else ""
        hosts = _dedupe([cache, bes])

        flags = []
        wired = []
        if cache:
            flags.append("--remote_cache=" + _SCHEME + d.cache)
            wired.append("remote cache")
        if bes:
            flags.append("--bes_backend=" + _SCHEME + d.bes)
            if d.results_url:
                flags.append("--bes_results_url=" + d.results_url)
            wired.append("BES")
        flags.extend(credential_helper_flags(hosts, credential_helper))
        if bes:
            flags.extend(bes_completeness_flags(exec_log_path))
        configs.append(RcConfig(
            name = name,
            comment = _label(d) + ": " + " + ".join(wired) + "; " + _login_hint(d) + ".",
            flags = flags,
        ))

        exec_name = ""
        if d.exec:
            exec_name = name + _EXEC_SUFFIX
            exec_host = endpoint_host(d.exec)
            exec_flags = ["--config=" + name, "--remote_executor=" + _SCHEME + d.exec]
            if exec_host not in hosts:
                exec_flags.extend(credential_helper_flags([exec_host], credential_helper))
            configs.append(RcConfig(
                name = exec_name,
                comment = "--config=" + name + " plus its remote execution.",
                flags = exec_flags,
            ))

        if d.default:
            aliases.append(RcConfig(
                name = DEFAULT_CONFIG,
                comment = "The default deployment (`aspect auth use`): " + _label(d) + ".",
                flags = ["--config=" + name],
            ))
            if exec_name:
                aliases.append(RcConfig(
                    name = DEFAULT_CONFIG + _EXEC_SUFFIX,
                    flags = ["--config=" + exec_name],
                ))
    return configs + aliases

def bes_completeness_flags(exec_log_path: str = "") -> list:
    """Flags that make a BES-wired invocation report everything the Aspect backend
    can use: every action's event (Bazel only publishes failed ones by default),
    every BEP-referenced local file uploaded to the remote cache (Bazel 7 flipped
    the default to `minimal`; 6.x already uploads all), the compact execution log
    (Bazel >= 7.1) when a path is given, and no early exit before the upload
    completes.

    Public (not `_`-prefixed) so `bazelrc_test.axl` can load it."""
    flags = [
        "--build_event_publish_all_actions",
        "--bes_upload_mode=wait_for_upload_complete",
        ("--remote_build_event_upload=all", ">=7.0.0"),
    ]
    if exec_log_path:
        flags.append(("--execution_log_compact_file=" + exec_log_path, ">=7.1.0"))
    return flags

def render_bazelrc(startup_flags: list, build_flags: list, command_sections: list, configs: list = []) -> str:
    """Render the managed block: markers, a `startup` line per startup flag, every
    build flag under each section in `command_sections` (`["common"]` on modern
    Bazel, `["build", "query"]` on Bazel < 6.3.0), then each `RcConfig` as a
    commented `<section>:<name>` group. Flags may be `(flag, condition)` tuples
    (the shape `rc.expand` yields for version-gated options); only the flag text
    is written."""
    lines = [
        BEGIN_MARKER + " — managed block, regenerated on every run; do not edit.",
        "# Configures vanilla `bazel` calls to use Aspect services and recommended optimizations.",
        "",
    ]
    for flag in startup_flags:
        lines.append("startup " + _flag_str(flag))
    for flag in build_flags:
        for section in command_sections:
            lines.append(section + " " + _flag_str(flag))
    for config in configs:
        lines.append("")
        if config.comment:
            lines.append("# " + config.comment)
        for flag in config.flags:
            for section in command_sections:
                lines.append(section + ":" + config.name + " " + _flag_str(flag))
    lines.append(END_MARKER)
    return "\n".join(lines) + "\n"

def merge_managed_block(existing: str | None, block: str) -> str:
    """The rc file content after placing `block` (a `render_bazelrc` result) into
    `existing`: replacing a previous block between the markers in place, replacing
    the whole file when it is an older marker-less `aspect ci bazelrc` output, and
    otherwise appending after the existing content. `None`/empty `existing` is a
    new file.

    Public (not `_`-prefixed) so `bazelrc_test.axl` can load it."""
    if not existing:
        return block
    lines = existing.split("\n")
    begin = [i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if line.startswith(BEGIN_MARKER)]
    end = [i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if line.startswith(END_MARKER)]
    if begin and end and end[-1] > begin[0]:
        before = "\n".join(lines[:begin[0]])
        after = "\n".join(lines[end[-1] + 1:])
        return (before + "\n" if before else "") + block + after
    if existing.startswith(_LEGACY_HEADER):
        return block
    return existing.rstrip("\n") + "\n\n" + block

def _default_output(ctx: TaskContext) -> str | None:
    """Default rc destination: `~/.bazelrc`. None (with an error) when the home
    directory can't be resolved and no `--output` was given."""
    home = ctx.std.env.home_dir()
    if home == None:
        error(ctx.std, "Could not resolve your home directory to default the output path. Pass --output=<path> explicitly.")
        return None
    return home.rstrip("/") + "/.bazelrc"

def _resolve(ctx: TaskContext, flags: list, bazel_version: str | None) -> list:
    """Resolve the version-gated `(flag, constraint)` tuples in `flags` against the
    detected Bazel version via the bazelrc runtime: a blank RunCommand whose
    `common` bucket holds every flag, expanded assumed-latest when the version is
    unknown. Config chain entries are kept verbatim ahead of the rest — the blank
    RunCommand has no section for them to expand into."""
    chain = [f for f in flags if is_config_chain(f)]
    rest = [f for f in flags if not is_config_chain(f)]
    rc = ctx.bazel.new_rc(flags = rest, version = bazel_version)
    return chain + rc.expand(command = "common")

def _exec_log_path(ctx: TaskContext) -> str:
    """A job-scoped location for the compact execution log the BES-wired configs
    write, under the OS temp dir so nothing lands in the checkout. Namespaced by
    this run's task id, since concurrent jobs on one machine share the temp dir."""
    dir = ctx.std.env.temp_dir().rstrip("/") + "/aspect-bazelrc-" + (ctx.task.id or "exec")
    ctx.std.fs.create_dir_all(dir)
    return dir + "/exec.log.zstd"

def _bazelrc_impl(ctx: TaskContext) -> int:
    environment = get_workflows_environment(ctx.std)
    on_runner = is_aspect_workflows_runner(ctx.std.env)
    explicit_output = bool(ctx.args.output)

    # Off a runner and off CI, don't write ~/.bazelrc by default — it's the
    # developer's own. Require an explicit --output there. On CI/runner, expected.
    if not on_runner and detect_ci(ctx.std.env) == None and not explicit_output:
        error(ctx.std, "Not on an Aspect Workflows runner or other CI. Not writing ~/.bazelrc by default off CI; pass --output=<path> to write somewhere explicit.")
        return 1

    if on_runner:
        # Full set: generic CI flags + the runner-specific cache/identity/output
        # flags. Gate on the runner metadata being present.
        if environment.runner == None:
            error(ctx.std, "Running on an Aspect Workflows runner but the runner metadata env vars are missing, so the cache flags cannot be generated. This usually means an older runner image; upgrade the runner.")
            return 1
        (startup_flags, build_flags) = get_bazelrc_flags(
            environment = environment,
            aspect_root_dir = ctx.std.env.aspect_root_dir(),
        )
        startup_flags = startup_flags_for_rc(startup_flags)
    else:
        # Off a runner (CI, or explicit --output): only the generic flags that
        # don't depend on the runner's mounts, identity, or the Workflows cache.
        # The remote-cache endpoint flags are still picked up from env vars when
        # set. No runner-specific startup flags.
        build_flags = get_generic_bazelrc_flags(environment)
        startup_flags = []

    bazel_version = ctx.bazel.version()
    build_flags = _resolve(ctx, build_flags, bazel_version)

    # The running binary is the credential helper: it certainly exists, whereas
    # a bare `aspect` on PATH may not for a later `bazel` step.
    configs = [
        RcConfig(name = c.name, comment = c.comment, flags = _resolve(ctx, c.flags, bazel_version))
        for c in deployment_configs(ctx.aspect.auth.list(), ctx.std.env.current_exe(), _exec_log_path(ctx))
    ]

    output = ctx.args.output if explicit_output else _default_output(ctx)
    if output == None:
        return 1

    block = render_bazelrc(startup_flags, build_flags, command_sections(bazel_version), configs)

    parent = output.rstrip("/").rsplit("/", 1)
    if len(parent) == 2 and parent[0] and not ctx.std.fs.exists(parent[0]):
        ctx.std.fs.create_dir_all(parent[0])
    existing = ctx.std.fs.read_to_string(output) if ctx.std.fs.exists(output) else None
    ctx.std.fs.write(output, merge_managed_block(existing, block))

    placed = "Replaced the Aspect bazelrc block in" if existing and BEGIN_MARKER in existing else ("Appended the Aspect bazelrc block to" if existing else "Wrote Aspect bazelrc to")
    summary = "%s %s (%d build flags, %d startup flags)" % (placed, output, len(build_flags), len(startup_flags))
    if configs:
        summary += "; --config sections: " + ", ".join([c.name for c in configs]) + "."
    else:
        summary += "; no --config sections, since no deployment advertises endpoints here (see `aspect auth status`; `aspect auth login` records Aspect Cloud's)."
    info(ctx.std, summary)
    return 0

bazelrc = task(
    group = ["ci"],
    summary = "Write a Bazel rc block that points vanilla `bazel` calls at Aspect's remote services and recommended optimizations.",
    description = "Write a Bazel rc block so vanilla `bazel` calls pick up the same configuration that `aspect <task>` injects. Unconditionally: the recommended CI/profiling flags, plus on an Aspect Workflows runner its remote cache, repository cache, and per-runner output paths. Opt-in `--config` sections for every Aspect deployment this machine knows (`aspect auth status`): `--config=aspect-cloud` for Aspect Cloud's remote cache + BES, `--config=aspect-<name>` for a configured deployment, `--config=aspect-<name>-exec` to add its remote execution, and `--config=aspect` for the default deployment — authenticated through the `aspect get` credential helper. Defaults to `~/.bazelrc`, replacing a previous block in place or appending to an existing file; off a runner and off CI it writes nothing unless `--output` is given, so it won't clobber your local `~/.bazelrc`.",
    implementation = _bazelrc_impl,
    args = {
        "output": args.string(
            default = "",
            description = "Rc file to write. Defaults to `~/.bazelrc` (the first user rc Bazel loads). Parent directories are created if needed. Only file output is supported — there is no stdout mode.",
        ),
    },
)
